parts.text:
Now I have enough context. Let me create a todo list and implement.

Plan:
1. relay/zen-relay.mjs: fold tool_calls + real usage; don't error when only tool calls; return them in completionJson; keep API compatible.
2. js/ai.js:
   - `openAICompat`: normalize `content` parts → text; detect `tool_calls` and raise a clear error (with tool names) when the model asks for tools; also detect degenerate text.
   - export helpers for tests: `textOf` (already there, not exported — export it), `sanitizeModelText` / `describeToolCalls`.
   - `chatWithImage`: use textOf for m.content (avoid "[object Object]"/"null").
3. js/chat.js:
   - don't send empty-content turns (filter history), and normalize the answer (String → text); show a clear message when the model returns nothing usable.
4. css/ui.css: nav labels don't break mid-word.
5. tests/smoke.mjs: add regression tests (numbered [32], [33]...).
6. README: document the tool-call behavior for the free tier.
7. version bump to 1.1.8, commit, push, tag v1.1.8 (triggers Pages + APK + release).

Let me start with the relay.

For sseFoldChat, implement:

```js
export function sseFoldChat(raw) {
  let content = '';
  let finish_reason = 'stop';
  let err = null;
  let usage = null;
  const calls = new Map(); // index -> {id, type, function:{name, arguments}}
  for (const line of raw.split(/\r?\n/)) {
    ...
      if (o.usage) usage = o.usage;
      const d = o.choices && o.choices[0];
      if (!d) continue;
      if (d.delta) {
        if (typeof d.delta.content === 'string') content += d.delta.content;
        if (Array.isArray(d.delta.tool_calls)) foldToolCalls(calls, d.delta.tool_calls);
      }
      if (d.finish_reason) finish_reason = d.finish_reason;
  }
  const tool_calls = [...calls.entries()].sort((a,b)=>a[0]-b[0]).map(([,c])=>c);
  const result = { content, finish_reason, usage };
  if (tool_calls.length) result.tool_calls = tool_calls;
  if (err) return {...result, finish_reason:'error', error: errText(err)};
  if (finish_reason === 'length') return {..., error: '...'};
  if (!content.trim() && !tool_calls.length) return {..., error: 'модель вернула пустой ответ'};
  return result;
}
```

Note: the existing test expects `r.content === 'Привет' && !r.error` for a normal reply — still fine. And `relay.sseFoldChat(sse('data: {"choices":[{"delta":{},"finish_reason":"length"}]}')).error` matches /лимит длины/ — fine. And `sseFoldChat(sse('data: [DONE]')).error` — empty stream, no tool calls → error. Fine.

foldToolCalls:
```js
function foldToolCalls(acc, deltas) {
  for (const d of deltas) {
    if (!d) continue;
    const i = Number.isInteger(d.index) ? d.index : acc.size;
    let c = acc.get(i);
    if (!c) { c = { id: '', type: 'function', function: { name: '', arguments: '' } }; acc.set(i, c); }
    if (d.id) c.id = d.id;
    if (d.type) c.type = d.type;
    const f = d.function || {};
    if (f.name) c.function.name += f.name;   // streamed names come whole usually
    if (typeof f.arguments === 'string') c.function.arguments += f.arguments;
  }
}
```

completionJson: add tool_calls and content null when only tool calls:
```js
export function completionJson(model, result) {
  const msg = { role: 'assistant', content: result.content || '' };
  if (result.tool_calls && result.tool_calls.length) {
    msg.tool_calls = result.tool_calls;
    if (!msg.content) msg.content = null;
  }
  return { ... };
}
```
Careful: existing test does `relay.completionJson('m', { content: 'x', usage: {...} })` — fine.

Hmm, one consideration: `usageOf(result)` currently falls back to char estimate; with real usage passed it uses real. Good.

Now, the client's error message. In `openAICompat`, after `const j = await r.json()`:
```js
const msg = (j.choices && j.choices[0] && j.choices[0].message) || {};
let out = textOf(msg.content);
const calls = Array.isArray(msg.tool_calls) ? msg.tool_calls : [];
if (calls.length) throw toolCallsError(name, model, calls, out);
```
Wait, but should we throw even if there's text? If there's text, we could return the text and warn on console. Best UX: if there is usable text → return the text (the chat shows it) but log a warning. If there is NO text (pure tool call) → throw a clear error naming the tools. Hmm, but then the user sees a "half" answer like "Давайте сначала посмотрим..." which is a lie — nothing will be looked at. Given the app is a chat (no tools), any tool call means the model's plan is unexecutable. I think: always surface it — if there's text, return text + append a note? No, don't fabricate model text.

Decision: throw an error whenever `tool_calls` are present, with a clear message that includes the tool names and the fact that VoiceComic's chat has no tools. Reason: silently returning the "let me look" text is what led to the garbage in the screenshot. But hmm — for models like big-pickle in *other* call sites (script generation, OCR) a throw would break the app's main features for keyless users! E.g. `chat(settings, ..., {json:true})` for script generation: the model may answer with a tool call → error "модель запросила инструменты". That's honest and better than garbage. And the error message tells the user what to do (choose another model / use a key).

Hmm, but wait: this would degrade the keyless UX significantly if these models ALWAYS call tools for app tasks. Let me test: ask ling to do a VoiceComic task (e.g. "придумай 3 реплики для панели комикса, ответь JSON") and see if it calls tools. If the model answers the actual task with text and no tool calls, then throwing only affects agent-flavored questions ("создай файл", "посмотри папку") — which is exactly the screenshot's case.

Let me test that quickly. This is important for choosing the behavior.

